<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-title">
      <h2>Creator Tool Directory</h2>
      <p>A small, practical set of tools for planning, writing, publishing, and reviewing posts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="recommendation-box" style="margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);">
      <p><strong>Disclosure:</strong> This page is an editorial resource, not a ranking guarantee. Tool names, prices, and features can change, so review each provider before buying. If affiliate links are added in the future, they will be clearly disclosed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tools-grid">
      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Analytics</span>
        <h3>X Analytics</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Checking impressions, engagement, profile visits, and follower signals from native data.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Do not judge every post by impressions alone. Compare metrics by post type.</p>
        <a href="https://analytics.x.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit X Analytics →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Scheduling</span>
        <h3>Typefully</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Drafting threads, previewing posts, and scheduling X-first content workflows.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Scheduling helps consistency, but it does not replace replying after publishing.</p>
        <a href="https://typefully.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Typefully →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Scheduling</span>
        <h3>Buffer</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Simple scheduling across multiple social accounts and lightweight planning.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Use it for publishing rhythm, not for automating away conversation.</p>
        <a href="https://buffer.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Buffer →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Writing</span>
        <h3>Hemingway App</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Tightening long sentences and spotting hard-to-read phrasing.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Clear writing is not always short writing. Keep nuance when it matters.</p>
        <a href="https://hemingwayapp.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Hemingway →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Design</span>
        <h3>Canva</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Creating simple carousel slides, checklists, and visual examples.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Keep text large enough for mobile. A crowded visual will not help the post.</p>
        <a href="https://canva.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Canva →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Research</span>
        <h3>Google Trends</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Checking whether a topic is seasonal, growing, or losing interest.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Trends should inform your examples, not replace your audience strategy.</p>
        <a href="https://trends.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Google Trends →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Audience</span>
        <h3>SparkToro</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Understanding where an audience spends attention and what sources they trust.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Use audience research to sharpen positioning, not to copy competitors.</p>
        <a href="https://sparktoro.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit SparkToro →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-card">
        <span class="tool-tag">Planning</span>
        <h3>Google Sheets</h3>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Maintaining a simple content calendar and weekly analytics review sheet.</p>
        <p><strong>Watch out:</strong> Track only metrics you will use. Too many columns make review harder.</p>
        <a href="https://sheets.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="tool-link">Visit Google Sheets →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

